{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::374291",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which are involved in Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity, a critical metabolic process in the electron transport chain. This activity is ultimately linked to Ndufs7, suggesting a potential role for Metformin in modulating the function of the Ndufs7 complex. The evidence indicates that Metformin may influence the activity of these enzymes through binding, which could alter the functional state of Ndufs7. The overlapping participation of Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 in the same metabolic pathway supports the idea that Metformin's effects on these targets may have a broader impact on the Ndufs7 complex. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Metformin could influence mitochondrial function, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
